		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=15622#p15622"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Merci rjuju,</p><p>&#160; J&#039;avai mis de côté cette problématique la semaine derniére, j&#039;y reviens aujourd&#039;hui:</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION recup_index()
RETURNS void
AS $BODY$
DECLARE
test CURSOR FOR SELECT attrelid from pg_attribute where attrelid in (select oid from pg_class where relname in (select indexname from pg_indexes));
oid int;
BEGIN
oid := 0;
for oid in test loop
COPY (SELECT pg_get_indexdef(oid)) TO &#039;\xxxxxxxx\test2.copy&#039;;
end loop;
return;
end;
$BODY$
LANGUAGE plpgsql;</code></pre></div><p>&#160; &#160;Suis je bien sur la bonne piste ? j&#039;ai toujours une erreur:</p><p>opsnetv3=&gt; \i recupindex.sql<br />psql:recupindex.sql:15: ERROR:&#160; syntax error at or near &quot;$1&quot;<br />LINE 1:&#160; &#160;$1<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ^<br />QUERY:&#160; &#160; $1<br />CONTEXT:&#160; SQL statement in PL/PgSQL function &quot;recup_index&quot; near line 6</p><p>Merci encore.</p>]]></content>
